Two-dimensional input (design 4.2 to 4.6, decision NB5.3): the typesetting keys in Input cells. A plain Input cell
becomes typeset at its first structure key; its text is canonical box text (4.4) and `--- boxes` gives the tree with
the caret (`▮`) or selection in the box notation.

=== Ctrl+/ makes a fraction of the operand before the caret (a `*` joins a box and a name, NBB.14)
--- before
#% cell
1+x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "Q" Ctrl+Space "Z"
--- after
#% cell typeset
1+((x)/(Q))*Z▮
--- boxes
1+(x/Q)*Z▮

=== Ctrl+/ on a selection makes it the numerator
--- before
#% cell
⟦1+x⟧
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "2"
--- boxes
(1+x/2▮)

=== Ctrl+6 and Ctrl+^ make a superscript
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+6 "2" Ctrl+Space "+y" Ctrl+^ "n"
--- after
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))+((y)^(n))▮
--- boxes
(x^2)+(y^n▮)

=== Ctrl+- and Ctrl+_ make a subscript
--- before
#% cell
a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+- "i" Ctrl+Space "+b" Ctrl+_ "j"
--- boxes
(a_i)+(b_j▮)

=== Ctrl+2 and Ctrl+@ insert a square root
--- before
#% cell
1+▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "x" Ctrl+Space "+" Ctrl+@ "y"
--- after
#% cell typeset
1+((sqrt(x)))+((sqrt(y)))▮
--- boxes
1+√(x)+√(y▮)

=== Ctrl+5 switches between the scripts
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+^ "2" Ctrl+5 "i"
--- boxes
((x_i▮)^2)

=== Ctrl+% switches too
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+_ "k" Ctrl+% "3"
--- boxes
((x_k)^3▮)

=== Tab goes to the next placeholder, Shift+Tab to the previous
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ Tab "B" Shift+Tab
--- boxes
(⟦□⟧/B)

=== Ctrl+, makes a grid column, Ctrl+Enter in a grid a row (the caret stays in its column)
--- before
#% cell
a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+, "b" Ctrl+Enter "c"
--- after
#% cell typeset
(([[a, b], [□, c]]))▮

=== Esc name Esc inserts a Greek letter
--- before
#% cell
((x)^(2))▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ Esc "alpha" Esc
--- boxes
((x^2)/α▮)

=== Esc int Esc is the integral sign, Esc intt Esc in a plain cell makes it typeset with an integral template
--- before
#% cell
▮
--- keys
Esc "int" Esc "+" Esc "intt" Esc "f"
--- after
#% cell typeset
∫+((integrate(f, □)))▮
--- boxes
∫+∫[□](f▮)

=== Esc sumt Esc after a box inserts a sum template
--- before
#% cell
1+▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "x" Ctrl+Space Esc "sumt" Esc
--- boxes
1+√(x)*∑[⟦□⟧=□..□](□)

=== Up moves from the denominator to the numerator
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a" Up "z"
--- boxes
(xz▮/a)

=== Left past the start goes to the insertion point before the cell
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a" Left Left Left Left Left
--- after
‖
#% cell typeset
((x)/(a))
--- boxes
none

=== Right past the end goes to the insertion point after the cell
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+^ "2" Right Right
--- after
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2))
‖
--- boxes
none

=== Backspace in boxes
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "ab" Backspace
--- boxes
(x/a▮)

=== undo goes back to the text before the structure
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "y" Ctrl+Z Ctrl+Z
--- after
#% cell
x▮

=== implicit multiplication stays visible
--- before
#% cell
a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+2 "b"
--- boxes
a*√(b▮)

=== Ctrl+Shift+N converts linear input to typeset input
--- before
#% cell
x^2 + sqrt(y)/3▮
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+N
--- after
#% cell typeset
((x)^(2)) + ((((sqrt(y))))/(3))▮

=== Ctrl+Shift+I converts typeset input back to linear text
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "a+b" Ctrl+Shift+I
--- after
#% cell
x/(a+b)▮

=== Ctrl+Shift+N on input that does not parse beeps and changes nothing
--- before
#% cell
f(▮
--- keys
Ctrl+Shift+N
--- after
#% cell
f(▮

=== evaluating a typeset cell sends its canonical text
--- before
#% cell
6▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "3" Shift+Enter
--- after
#% cell label=1 typeset
((6)/(3))
#% output n=1
#= ((6)/(3))
‖

=== structure keys in a Text cell do nothing
--- before
#% text
# a▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/
--- after
#% text
# a▮
--- boxes
none

=== copy in boxes copies canonical text, which pastes back as boxes
--- before
#% cell
x▮
--- keys
Ctrl+/ "y" Ctrl+A Ctrl+C Right Ctrl+V
--- boxes
(x/y)*(x/y)▮
